## Nonprod Flow

The desired nonprod flow is approximately:

```text
Build image
    |
Validate tooling / .NET
    |
Security scan
    |
Push to Nonprod ACR
    |
Trigger Nonprod Spacelift
    |
Terraform + Helm deployment
    |
Wait for deployment success
    |
Run existing nonprod validation
```

If the current workflow already performs additional validation, preserve it.

Possible validation may include:

- runner pod starts
- runner registers with GitHub
- test workflow can execute
- .NET builds work on the actual deployed runner
- runtime security scan passes
- required CLI tooling works

The exact validation should follow the existing implementation and organizational requirements.

---

## Production Flow

After nonprod is successfully validated:

```text
Approved nonprod image
        |
        v
Promote to Prod ACR
        |
        v
Trigger Prod Spacelift
        |
        v
Terraform + Helm
        |
        v
Prod ARC
```

Reuse the existing image promotion method if it already safely promotes the same validated artifact.

Do not introduce a rebuild just because the deployment mechanism changes to Spacelift.

---

## Failure Behavior

Preserve a fail-closed release model.

Examples:

```text
build fails
    -> stop

security scan fails
    -> stop

nonprod deployment fails
    -> stop

nonprod validation fails
    -> stop before promotion

image promotion fails
    -> stop

prod deployment fails
    -> report deployment failure
```

Do not allow production deployment to continue after an earlier release gate fails.

---

## Implementation Approach

Make changes incrementally.

Suggested order:

### Step 1

Understand and document the existing workflow.

Do not modify anything yet.

### Step 2

Identify the exact point where GitHub currently performs the nonprod Terraform/Helm deployment.

Determine how that can be replaced by or delegated to the existing nonprod Spacelift stack.

### Step 3

Prove GitHub can:

```text
trigger nonprod Spacelift
        ->
wait for result
        ->
continue existing workflow
```

without changing the rest of the pipeline.

### Step 4

Verify the expected image/tag/digest reaches Terraform and ARC correctly.

### Step 5

Preserve and test the existing nonprod validation steps.

### Step 6

Integrate the existing production promotion/deployment flow with the production Spacelift stack.

### Step 7

Only after the basic integration works, consider improvements such as:

- digest pinning
- workload identity / OIDC
- SBOM generation
- image signing
- stronger Spacelift policies
- production approvals
- external dependencies
- automated rollback

These should not block understanding or integrating the existing system.

